a:
Secular education keeps public education free of religious dominance. It is needed:
1. to remove narrow-mindedness and give an enlightened view;
2. to develop a moral and humanistic outlook;
3. to train youth to be good citizens;
4. to strengthen democratic values of liberty, equality, fraternity and co-operative living;
5. to give a wider vision of life;
6. to develop understanding of others' points of view;
7. to develop love, tolerance, co-operation and sympathy;
8. to combine materialism and spiritualism.
